    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d170-a2">

                <pb facs="0536" n="478" sameAs="frus:frus1866p3/pg478"/>

                <head>Mr. Mathieu to Mr.
                        Burton</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 25.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Consulate of the United States</hi>,
                                <hi rendition="#italic">Cartagena</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1865-08-28"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >August</hi> 28, 1865.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: In answer to your private note of the 13th
                    instant, I have to report to you officially that Julian J. Berrios, who, in
                    March, 1864, ordered the steamer Antioquia to be fired into, <pb facs="0537"
                        n="479" xml:id="pg479"/> has been, during three or four months, contactor
                    general del estado—that is, as far as September or October, 1864; that he was
                    appointed governor of the province of Magangue, and was governor when the late
                    revolution broke out; and, finally, that he is now in Ocaña, or its
                    neighborhood. He is called Doctor Berrios, not a pyhsician, but a lawyer, and
                    was born in that part of the country.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, very respectfully, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>ALBERT MATHIEU, <hi rendition="#italic">United States
                        Vice-Consul</hi>.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Allan</hi> A. <hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Burton, Bogota</hi>.</p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
